load @term/seed/code/structure/space/vector
  find vector-space

# An algebraic variety: the set of common zeros of a collection of polynomials, the geometric shape cut out by
# polynomial equations. It is the central object of algebraic geometry, the bridge where algebra (the polynomials) and
# geometry (their solution set) become one. A variety is irreducible when it is not the union of two smaller varieties.
# The form carries the ambient vector space; the defining polynomials and their zero locus are the content.
form algebraic-variety
  link space, like vector-space
